  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "ATV320 Book (ATV320...B) and Compact (ATV320...C) drives on the built-in RJ45 Modbus serial port; register map per Communication Parameters file NVE41316 V3.5.",
  "summary": "Schneider Electric's machine-oriented variable frequency drive with Modbus RTU built into the RJ45 port on the control block. Every parameter has a fixed decimal logical address that is sent unchanged as the holding-register address. This map covers the CiA402 command/status words (CMD/ETA), frequency and speed references, the main monitors (output frequency, current, voltages, thermal states, power), fault codes and history, I/O states, and the Modbus and channel settings needed to put the drive under network control.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Logical addresses are decimal (the parameter file also shows hex as 16#....) and go into the request unchanged. The Modbus manual's read example asks for W3102-W3105 by sending starting address 0C1E hex (= 3102), and its write example writes W9001 at 2329 hex. So ETA 3201 is requested at address 3201 (0x0C81), with no 40001 offset and no minus 1."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "ATV320 - Communication Parameters (Excel)",
    "doc_number": "NVE41316 V3.5",
    "revision_date": "2024-09",
    "url": "https://download.schneider-electric.com/files?p_Doc_Ref=NVE41316",
    "pages": "Sheet 'Parameters' (code, logic address, type, unit, access), sheet 'Registers' (CMI/CMD/ETA/ETI/CRC/CCC/IL1R/OL1R/UNT bits), sheet 'Enumerations' (HMIS, LFT, CHCF, ECFG, PSA, CDX, TBR, FOR, INR, STT). Also: Altivar Machine ATV320 Modbus Serial Link Manual NVE41308 (04/2016) pp. 17-21 functions and examples, pp. 31-37 settings and scanner, pp. 46-49 CMD/ETA, p. 66 SLL, pp. 77-80 channel monitoring."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Second source: Altivar Machine ATV320 Modbus Serial Link Manual NVE41308 rev 01 (04/2016), https://download.schneider-electric.com/files?p_Doc_Ref=NVE41308 - used for addressing, function codes, the Add/tbr/tFO/ttO settings, the CiA402 sequence and SLL behaviour.",
    "Every register is a single 16-bit word; the map has no 32-bit values.",
    "M1EC (6010) and M1CT (6011) are not in the parameter file; their logical addresses come from the Modbus manual p. 74.",
    "LFR (8502) and RFR (3202) are 0.1 Hz only while CMI bit 9 = 0 (power-up default); with bit 9 = 1 they become a signed value where 32767 = tFr.",
    "APH, RTH and PTH have no fixed unit: read UNT (3234) after them to learn whether each is in Wh/kWh/MWh or s/min/h.",
    "ACC/DEC are raw values; their resolution follows INR (9020): 0 = 0.01 s, 1 = 0.1 s (factory), 2 = 1 s.",
    "LFT and DP0-DP3 use the full LFT list (61 codes) from the parameter file Enumerations sheet.",
    "FR1 and CD1 value lists show the channel choices relevant to network control; the full PSA list also includes analog and function sources.",
    "Left out: ERRD (CiA402 error code, 8606) because the file types it as a bit string but gives a code list; CCS (8421) values because they come from a long assignable-input list; option-card (CANopen, Ethernet, EtherCAT) parameters; Safety-function and function-block registers.",
    "Registers marked RW that the source lists as R/WS can only be written while the drive is not running (not in Operation enabled or Quick stop active)."
  ],
